Chapter: CollideAlpha

 Two chapters in one compilation unit each define collide-helper, with
 the same type and different answers. This is legal and it compiles, and
 that is the whole problem: ChapterScoper mangles both, each chapter
 keeps its own, and nothing in either file says the name is contested.

 The warning under test is CDX3006, raised once at each definition site.
 It is a warning and not an error because a collision is sometimes
 deliberate, so this test must COMPILE and RUN, not fail.

 The runtime answer is the second half of the claim. CollideBeta's
 opening calls collide-helper without qualification and gets BETA's
 definition, because a mention resolves in the chapter it sits in. Move
 that same line into CollideAlpha and it would answer 2 instead of 101,
 with no diagnostic and no textual difference.

Section: Alpha
  collide-helper : Integer -> Integer
  collide-helper (n) = n + 1

Chapter: CollideBeta

 The other half of the pair.

Section: Beta
  collide-helper : Integer -> Integer
  collide-helper (n) = n + 100

Section: Entry
  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni ("collide-helper 1 = " & show (collide-helper 1))
  end
